eative parts because they wanted  soldiers to become mindless war machines  but in order to do that you'd first need  to figure out how that part of the brain  works but to lock up the creative mind  we also have to understand how to unlock  it this is our first confirmation that  the chemist has ties to the us military  and with death valley the second part of  double feature heavily featuring the us  military the chemist and the black pill  are the strongest links we currently  have that connect the two parts in the  promo material we even see a pale  creature and alien ingesting the black  pill we also don't know what exactly is  in one of these pills could the missing  ingredient be something not of this  world but then that begs the question  how has she been able to make these  pills for the last five years without  running out of this special alien  ingredient unless of course she herself  is not of this world in episode 3 she  tells mickey and belle noir that if she  were to die the secret of the pill would  die with her we learned that the chemist  was involved in testing the black pill  on primates and that it stimulates the  occipital lobe of the brain the part  which controls creativity users who take  it can experience 10 50 or even a  thousand times the function of this lobe  while on the drug the downside is that  some of the apes became highly  aggressive and tore the other apes limb  from limb it's almost like the  non-creative ones can tolerate their  lack of talent  until they're confronted with it  then their mediocrity drives a man  mickey is like hell no i ain't taking  that drug and the chemist offers him 50  bucks for any test subjects he brings to  her so that night while he's with tb  karen he asks her if she has any talent  to which she says  no i'm [ __ ] inside and now can i have a  hit so karen's out of the mix but when  mickey finds the man who will later  become the pale creature singing he  quickly ushers him to the chemist the  fact