e of  these pills the chemist explains that  there will be side effects but bella is  willing to do anything and even agrees  to be monitored and studied by her that  night she finishes an entire book while  high off the drug it's reminiscent of  what happened to harry when he was doing  his work rey arrives later that morning  telling his wife he spent the night with  another woman and continues to berate  her this is the last straw for belle who  smashes a wine bottle slits his throat  and gorges off his blood she'll later  tell the chemist that it was like she  could smell the blood through his skin  the pale man turns more and more into  gollum visiting the chemist afraid of  how the drug is affecting him he says  he's freezing cold and the chemist shoes  him away telling him to get a coat we're  back at lark's shop which was actually  hinted as having a fine vintage rack in  the radio promotional material  hot tip that tattoo shop on commercial  street has a truly iconic vintage rack  so we get this great coat origin story  as lark explains there used to be a lot  of gay people here but when they left in  the late 80s they left their fashion  with them at the graveyard which seems  to be the pale man stomping ground he  performs his first kill on an  unsuspecting mourner as a vegan this is  very surprising to him the chemist tells  him that his urge to kill is caused by  two things a lack of minerals in the  body and rage a rage fueled by the  hatred he has for the world for giving  him dreams that were too big the  talented pill takers have this rage too  however for them their rage is caused by  their own arrogance and certainty that  they're better than everyone the pale  man's rage however is much darker and  more intense the chemist has to pull a  gun on the pale man whose rage boils  over and it's here she exclaims that 9  out of 10 people who take the pill will  turn out like him this may explain why  in episode 3 she turns down an offer  from ursula to 